<title>POLAND: RAFAKO CLAIMS PLN 19 MLN FLOOD PAYMENT.</title>
<headline>RAFAKO CLAIMS PLN 19 MLN FLOOD PAYMENT.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish industrial boilermaker Rafako SA demanded on Tuesday 19 million zlotys in flood damage compensation from the state, saying it had not been warned in time.</p>
<p>&quot;The company claims 19 million zlotys in compensation payments from the State Treasury....If we had been warned in due time of the forthcoming danger we might have saved most of the equipment,&quot; PAP news agency on Tuesday quoted Rafako deputy president Antoni Szendzielorz as saying.</p>
<p>Rafako's flood losses are estimated at 18.9 million zlotys.</p>
<p>Earlier this month the company said it would resume full production in September and that flood-related losses would not affect this year's sales forecast of 370 million zlotys.</p>
<p>PAP gave no further details, and no one at the firm was immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
